"""Source cards for the hadith that Hadi's older shelf answers already cite.

Each summary was written from the hadith text itself (fawazahmed0/hadith-api
English edition, read for this change), says only what that narration says, and
is shown to the person as "Summary written for this app, not a translation".
The grade and the grader come from the corpus, never from here.
"""
card('abudawud:1067', 'Tariq ibn Shihab: the Friday prayer in congregation is a duty on every Muslim, except a slave, a woman, a boy and a sick person.')
card('abudawud:1400', 'Abu Hurayrah: a surah of thirty verses, Surah al-Mulk, will intercede for its reader until he is forgiven.')
card('abudawud:1416', 'Ali: Allah is single (witr) and loves what is single, so pray the witr, you people of the Qur\'an.')
card('abudawud:1425', 'Al-Hasan ibn Ali: the Prophet taught him words to say in the witr supplication, beginning "O Allah, guide me among those You have guided".')
card('abudawud:162', 'Ali: if religion went by opinion, wiping the underside of the shoe would be more fitting than the top, but he saw the Prophet wipe the top of his shoes.')
card('abudawud:181', 'Busrah bint Safwan: the Prophet said whoever touches his private part should make wudu.')
card('abudawud:2130', 'Abu Hurayrah: to a man on his marriage the Prophet said "May Allah bless for you, bless upon you, and bring you together in good".')
card('abudawud:2838', 'Samurah: a boy is held in pledge for his aqiqah, which is sacrificed for him on the seventh day, with his head shaved and a name given.')
card('abudawud:3106', 'Ibn Abbas: whoever visits a sick person whose time has not come and says seven times "I ask Allah, the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to cure you", Allah will cure him.')
card('abudawud:3201', 'Abu Hurayrah: the Prophet\'s supplication at a funeral prayer, asking forgiveness for the living and the dead and for life in faith and death in Islam.')
card('abudawud:3641', 'Abu ad-Darda: whoever travels a road seeking knowledge, Allah makes a road to Paradise easy for him, and the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge.')
card('abudawud:3761', 'Salman al-Farsi: the blessing of food is in washing before and after it. Abu Dawud himself says this report is weak.')
card('abudawud:3764', 'Wahshi ibn Harb: the Companions said they ate and were not satisfied; the Prophet told them to eat together and mention Allah\'s name, and they would be blessed in it.')
card('abudawud:3767', 'Aisha: when one of you eats he should mention Allah\'s name; if he forgets at the start, he should say "In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end".')
card('abudawud:3850', 'Abu Said al-Khudri: after finishing food the Prophet said "Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink and made us Muslims".')
card('abudawud:4104', 'Aisha: the Prophet told Asma that once a woman reaches maturity nothing should be seen of her except her face and hands. Abu Dawud notes the chain is broken (mursal).')
card('abudawud:4811', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever does not thank people is not thankful to Allah.')
card('abudawud:4948', 'Abu ad-Darda: on the Day of Resurrection you will be called by your names and your fathers\' names, so give yourselves good names.')
card('abudawud:495', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: command your children to pray at seven, discipline them for it at ten, and separate their beds.')
card('abudawud:5045', 'Hafsah: when going to sleep the Prophet put his right hand under his cheek and said three times "O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants".')
card('abudawud:5088', 'Uthman ibn Affan: whoever says three times "In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing", will not be struck by sudden affliction that morning or evening.')
card('abudawud:5095', 'Anas: when a man leaves his house and says "In the name of Allah, I trust in Allah, there is no might or power but with Allah", it is said to him "You are guided, defended and protected".')
card('abudawud:5096', 'Abu Malik al-Ashari: on entering his home a man should say the supplication "O Allah, I ask You for the good of entering and leaving; in Allah\'s name we enter and leave and on Allah our Lord we rely", and then greet his family.')
card('abudawud:5105', 'Abu Rafi: he saw the Prophet give the call to prayer in the ear of al-Hasan ibn Ali when Fatimah gave birth to him.')

card('bukhari:1', 'Umar ibn al-Khattab: deeds are judged by intentions, and each person gets what he intended; the emigration for Allah and His Messenger differs from one made for worldly gain or a woman.')
card('bukhari:1032', 'Aisha: when the Prophet saw rain he would say "O Allah, make it a beneficial downpour".')
card('bukhari:106', 'Ali: the Prophet said "Do not tell lies about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire".')
card('bukhari:1129', 'Aisha: the Prophet prayed at night in the mosque and people joined him; after a few nights he stayed away, fearing that the prayer would become obligatory for them.')
card('bukhari:1166', 'Jabir: the Prophet taught the istikhara prayer for all matters, two rak\'ahs followed by the supplication "O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge".')
card('bukhari:1280', 'Zaynab bint Abi Salama, quoting the Prophet: a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day may not mourn more than three days for the dead, except four months and ten days for a husband.')
card('bukhari:1302', 'Anas: the Prophet said real patience is at the first stroke of a calamity.')
card('bukhari:1325', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever attends a funeral until he prays over the dead gets one qirat of reward, and whoever stays until burial gets two, each like a great mountain.')
card('bukhari:1385', 'Abu Hurayrah: every child is born on the fitrah, and his parents make him a Jew, a Christian or a Magian.')
card('bukhari:1395', 'Ibn Abbas: the Prophet sent Mu\'adh to Yemen and told him to call people to the testimony of faith, then to the five daily prayers, then to zakat, taken from their rich and given to their poor.')
card('bukhari:1403', 'Abu Hurayrah: the Prophet said that wealth whose zakat is not paid will on the Day of Resurrection become a bald, venomous snake that coils round its owner\'s neck; he then recited Qur\'an 3:180.')
card('bukhari:1417', 'Adi ibn Hatim: the Prophet said to protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date given in charity.')
card('bukhari:1427', 'Hakim ibn Hizam: the upper hand (giving) is better than the lower (taking); start with your dependents; the best charity is from what is left after your needs; and whoever avoids begging, Allah makes him self-sufficient.')
card('bukhari:1782', 'Ibn Abbas: the Prophet told an Ansari woman who had been unable to perform Hajj with him that Umrah in Ramadan equals Hajj in reward.')
card('bukhari:1909', 'Abu Hurayrah: fast when you see the new moon of Ramadan, stop fasting when you see the new moon of Shawwal, and if it is cloudy complete thirty days of Shaban.')
card('bukhari:2004', 'Ibn Abbas: the Prophet found the Jews of Madinah fasting on Ashura, the day Allah saved the Children of Israel; he said "We have more right to Musa than you", fasted it and told the Muslims to fast it.')
card('bukhari:2017', 'Aisha: the Prophet said to look for Laylat al-Qadr in the odd nights of the last ten days of Ramadan.')
card('bukhari:2025', 'Abdullah ibn Umar: the Prophet used to practise i\'tikaf in the last ten days of Ramadan.')
card('bukhari:2044', 'Abu Hurayrah: the Prophet used to make i\'tikaf for ten days each Ramadan, and in the year he died he stayed twenty days.')
card('bukhari:228', 'Aisha: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh asked whether she should stop praying because of continuous bleeding; the Prophet said it was from a vein, not menstruation, so she should leave prayer only for her real period, then wash and pray.')
card('bukhari:2311', 'Abu Hurayrah: while he guarded the zakat of Ramadan a thief came; he released him twice; the third time the thief taught him to recite Ayat al-Kursi at night for Allah\'s protection, and the Prophet said he had told the truth.')
card('bukhari:2320', 'Anas: no Muslim plants a tree or sows a field and then a bird, person or animal eats from it, except that it counts as charity for him.')
card('bukhari:2322', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever keeps a dog loses one qirat of his reward every day, unless it is for guarding crops or livestock, or for hunting.')
card('bukhari:2363', 'Abu Hurayrah: a man gave water to a thirsty dog and Allah thanked him for it and forgave him; the people asked whether there is reward in serving animals, and he said there is a reward in every living creature.')
card('bukhari:247', 'Al-Bara: the Prophet told him that at bedtime he should make wudu as for prayer, lie on his right side and say the supplication beginning "O Allah, I submit myself to You"; if he dies that night he dies in faith, on Islam.')
card('bukhari:2654', 'Abu Bakrah: the Prophet named the greatest sins as associating partners with Allah and disobeying parents, and then warned repeatedly against false witness.')
card('bukhari:2697', 'Aisha: whoever introduces into this matter of ours something that is not part of it, it is rejected.')
card('bukhari:2736', 'Abu Hurayrah: Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred less one, and whoever learns them will enter Paradise.')
card('bukhari:2742', 'Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: when ill he asked to bequeath his property; the Prophet refused half, allowed a third and said even a third is a lot, and that leaving his heirs well-off is better than leaving them poor.')
card('bukhari:28', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: asked which part of Islam is best, the Prophet said to feed people and to greet those you know and those you do not know.')
card('bukhari:294', 'Aisha: she began her period on the way to Hajj; the Prophet told her to do everything the pilgrims do except the tawaf round the Kaaba.')
card('bukhari:304', 'Abu Said al-Khudri: at the Eid prayer the Prophet told the women to give charity, said most of the people he had seen in Hell were women because of frequent cursing and ingratitude to husbands, and explained their "deficiency in religion" as not praying or fasting during their period.')
card('bukhari:306', 'Aisha: the Prophet told Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh, who had bleeding outside her period, to leave the prayer during her real period, then wash the blood off and pray.')
card('bukhari:3208', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: a person is gathered in the mother\'s womb for forty days, then a clot, then a piece of flesh, each for forty days, and then an angel is sent to write his provision, lifespan, deeds and whether he will be wretched or happy.')
card('bukhari:321', 'Muadha: Aisha said that women in the Prophet\'s time who had their period were not told to make up the prayers they missed.')
card('bukhari:3244', 'Abu Hurayrah: Allah says "I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard and no human heart has imagined".')
card('bukhari:3268', 'Aisha: magic was worked on the Prophet so that he imagined doing things he had not done; Allah told him in a dream who did it and how, and he was cured.')
card('bukhari:3276', 'Abu Hurayrah: Satan comes to one of you asking who created this and that, until he asks who created your Lord; when that happens, seek refuge in Allah and stop.')
card('bukhari:3281', 'Safiyyah: when two Ansari men passed as the Prophet walked her home, he told them it was his wife Safiyyah, adding that Satan moves in a person like blood and he feared a doubt would be cast into their hearts.')
card('bukhari:3292', 'Abu Qatadah: a good dream is from Allah and a disturbing one from Satan; whoever has a bad dream should spit lightly to his left and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, and it will not harm him.')
card('bukhari:33', 'Abu Hurayrah: the signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is trusted he betrays.')
card('bukhari:3365', 'Ibn Abbas: part of the story of Hajar and Ismail at Makkah, her running between Safa and Marwa and the coming of Zamzam; the Prophet said if she had let it flow it would have been a running spring.')
card('bukhari:3420', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: the Prophet said the most beloved fasting to Allah is that of Dawud, who fasted every other day, and the most beloved prayer is Dawud\'s, who slept half the night, prayed a third and slept a sixth.')
card('bukhari:344', 'Imran ibn Husayn: on a journey the people slept through the dawn prayer; a man in need of a major wash was told to do tayammum with clean earth and told it was enough for him, and later water was brought for him to pour over himself.')
card('bukhari:3461', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: convey from me even one verse, and relate from the Children of Israel, there is no harm in it; but whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.')
card('bukhari:38', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and hoping for reward, his past sins are forgiven.')
card('bukhari:4008', 'Abu Masud al-Badri: the last two verses of Surat al-Baqarah, recited at night, are enough for him.')
card('bukhari:401', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: when the Prophet prayed more than usual and was told, he made two prostrations (sujud as-sahw) and said he is a human being who forgets as they do.')
card('bukhari:4505', 'Ibn Abbas: the verse allowing those able to fast to feed a poor person instead (2:184) is not cancelled; it is for old men and women who cannot fast, who feed one poor person for each day.')
card('bukhari:4563', 'Ibn Abbas: "Allah is sufficient for us and the best Disposer of affairs" was said by Ibrahim when thrown into the fire and by Muhammad when told that people had gathered against them.')
card('bukhari:4937', 'Aisha: the one who is skilled in reciting the Qur\'an is with the noble, obedient angels, and the one who recites with difficulty and effort has a double reward.')
card('bukhari:4986', 'Zayd ibn Thabit: after many reciters died at Yamama, Umar urged Abu Bakr to have the Qur\'an collected, and Abu Bakr asked Zayd to gather it from written pieces and from memory.')
card('bukhari:50', 'Abu Hurayrah: the angel Jibril asked the Prophet about faith, Islam and ihsan, and the Prophet explained each; Islam is worshipping Allah alone, the prayer, zakat and fasting Ramadan.')
card('bukhari:5009', 'Abu Masud: whoever recites the last two verses of Surat al-Baqarah at night, they will be enough for him.')
card('bukhari:5013', 'Abu Said al-Khudri: a man kept repeating Surat al-Ikhlas and thought it little; the Prophet said, by Him in whose hand is my soul, it is equal to a third of the Qur\'an.')
card('bukhari:5017', 'Aisha: each night at bedtime the Prophet cupped his hands, blew into them after reciting Ikhlas, Falaq and Nas, and wiped over his body three times.')
card('bukhari:5027', 'Uthman: the best among you are those who learn the Qur\'an and teach it.')
card('bukhari:5173', 'Abdullah ibn Umar: if any of you is invited to a wedding feast, he should attend.')
card('bukhari:5469', 'Asma bint Abi Bakr: she gave birth to Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr at Quba; the Prophet chewed a date, put it in the baby\'s mouth (tahnik) and prayed for blessing for him.')
card('bukhari:5645', 'Abu Hurayrah: if Allah wants good for someone, He afflicts him with trials.')
card('bukhari:574', 'Abu Musa: whoever prays the two cool prayers, Asr and Fajr, will enter Paradise.')
card('bukhari:5740', 'Abu Hurayrah: the effect of the evil eye is real, and the Prophet forbade tattooing.')
card('bukhari:5763', 'Aisha: Labid ibn al-Asam of Banu Zuraiq worked magic on the Prophet so that he imagined doing things he had not done; Allah told him what had been done and how, and he was healed.')
card('bukhari:5889', 'Abu Hurayrah: five things are of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails, plucking the underarm hair and trimming the moustache.')
card('bukhari:5954', 'Aisha: the Prophet tore down a curtain with pictures and said those who imitate Allah\'s creation will be punished most severely on the Day of Resurrection.')
card('bukhari:6', 'Ibn Abbas: the Prophet was the most generous of people, and most generous in Ramadan when Jibril met him each night to review the Qur\'an with him.')
card('bukhari:6011', 'An-Numan ibn Bashir: believers in their mutual mercy, love and kindness are like one body; if one part complains, the whole body shares the sleeplessness and fever.')
card('bukhari:6013', 'Jarir ibn Abdullah: whoever is not merciful to people, Allah is not merciful to him.')
card('bukhari:6014', 'Aisha: the Prophet said Jibril kept advising him to be kind to the neighbour until he thought he would make the neighbour an heir.')
card('bukhari:6015', 'Ibn Umar: the Prophet said Jibril kept advising him to be kind to the neighbour until he thought he would make the neighbour an heir.')
card('bukhari:6018', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbour, should honour his guest, and should say what is good or keep silent.')
card('bukhari:6094', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: truthfulness leads to righteousness and righteousness leads to Paradise; lying leads to wickedness and wickedness leads to the Fire.')
card('bukhari:6114', 'Abu Hurayrah: the strong person is not the one who overpowers others but the one who controls himself in anger.')
card('bukhari:614', 'Jabir: whoever says the supplication after the call to prayer ("O Allah, Lord of this perfect call...") will be granted the Prophet\'s intercession on the Day of Resurrection.')
card('bukhari:6224', 'Abu Hurayrah: when one of you sneezes he should say "Praise be to Allah"; his brother replies "May Allah have mercy on you", and he answers "May Allah guide you and set your affairs right".')
card('bukhari:6306', 'Shaddad ibn Aws: the best way of asking forgiveness (sayyid al-istighfar) is "O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You..."; whoever says it with certainty by day and dies before evening will be among the people of Paradise.')
card('bukhari:6309', 'Anas: Allah is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you is on finding his lost camel in the desert.')
card('bukhari:631', 'Malik ibn al-Huwayrith: after staying twenty days with the Prophet, the young men were told to return to their families, teach them, and "pray as you have seen me pray".')
card('bukhari:6324', 'Hudhayfah: at bedtime the Prophet said "In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live", and on waking "Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection".')
card('bukhari:6369', 'Anas: the Prophet used to seek refuge in Allah from worry and grief, incapacity and laziness, cowardice and miserliness, heavy debt and being overpowered by men.')
card('bukhari:6446', 'Abu Hurayrah: wealth is not having many possessions; real wealth is contentment of the soul.')
card('bukhari:645', 'Abdullah ibn Umar: prayer in congregation is twenty-seven times better than the prayer of a person alone.')
card('bukhari:7352', 'Amr ibn al-As: when a judge strives and gets it right he has two rewards, and if he strives and errs he has one.')
card('bukhari:893', 'Ibn Umar: the Prophet said all of you are guardians and each is responsible for those under his care.')
card('bukhari:900', 'Ibn Umar: the Prophet said do not stop Allah\'s female servants from going to Allah\'s mosques; a wife of Umar used to attend the Fajr and Isha prayers for this reason.')
card('bukhari:935', 'Abu Hurayrah: the Prophet spoke of Friday and said there is an hour in it in which a Muslim who prays and asks Allah for something will be given it, and he indicated with his hand that it is short.')
card('bukhari:950', 'Aisha: on Eid two girls were singing the songs of Buath in her house; Abu Bakr objected but the Prophet said to leave them, because every people has a festival and this is ours.')
card('bukhari:986', 'Jabir: on the day of Eid the Prophet used to return by a different road from the one he went by.')
card('bukhari:990', 'Ibn Umar: the night prayer is two rak\'ahs at a time, and whoever fears the dawn should pray one rak\'ah to make the prayers odd.')

card('ibnmajah:1846', 'Aisha: marriage is part of my sunnah; whoever lacks the means should fast, for it reduces desire.')
card('ibnmajah:2719', 'Abu Hurayrah: learn the rules of inheritance and teach them, for they are half of knowledge and will be forgotten. (Graded weak.)')
card('ibnmajah:3062', 'Jabir: the water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for.')

card('muslim:101', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever takes up arms against us is not one of us, and whoever deceives us is not one of us.')
card('muslim:1015', 'Abu Hurayrah: Allah is good and accepts only what is good; He commanded the believers to eat of the good things, and a person whose food and drink are unlawful will not have his prayer answered.')
card('muslim:1051', 'Abu Hurayrah: richness is not having many possessions; true richness is richness of the soul.')
card('muslim:1095', 'Anas: take the pre-dawn meal (suhur), for there is blessing in it.')
card('muslim:1098', 'Sahl ibn Sad: people will continue to do well as long as they hasten to break the fast.')
card('muslim:1134', 'Ibn Abbas: the Prophet fasted Ashura and told people to fast it; when told the Jews and Christians honour it, he said that next year, if Allah wills, they would fast the ninth too, but he died before the next year.')
card('muslim:1163', 'Abu Hurayrah: the best fast after Ramadan is in Allah\'s month of Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory prayers is the night prayer.')
card('muslim:1169', 'Aisha: look for Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan.')
card('muslim:1172', 'Aisha: the Prophet used to make i\'tikaf in the last ten days of Ramadan until Allah took him, and his wives did so after him.')
card('muslim:1218', 'Jabir: the long account of the Prophet\'s Farewell Pilgrimage, from leaving Madinah through the rites at Arafat, Muzdalifah, Mina and the Kaaba.')
card('muslim:134', 'Abu Hurayrah: if people keep asking until they ask "Allah created all things, so who created Allah?", whoever meets this should say "I believe in Allah" and stop.')
card('muslim:1342', 'Ibn Umar: when setting out on a journey the Prophet said "Allahu akbar" three times and then the travel supplication "Glory to Him who subjected this to us".')
card('muslim:1349', 'Abu Hurayrah: one Umrah to the next wipes out what is between them, and an accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise.')
card('muslim:1350', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever performs Hajj and does not speak indecently or disobey returns free of sin, as on the day his mother bore him.')
card('muslim:1429', 'Ibn Umar: when any of you is invited to a feast he should accept.')
card('muslim:1574', 'Ibn Umar: whoever keeps a dog other than one for herding or hunting loses two qirats of his reward every day.')
card('muslim:16', 'Ibn Umar: Islam is built on five: that Allah is One (worship of Allah alone), establishing the prayer, paying zakat, fasting Ramadan and the pilgrimage to the House.')
card('muslim:1716', 'Amr ibn al-As: when a judge strives to reach the right judgment and is right he has two rewards, and if he errs he has one reward.')
card('muslim:1718', 'Aisha: whoever does an act that is not in accordance with our matter (the religion), it is rejected.')
card('muslim:1827', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: those who are just will be on pulpits of light beside Allah, those who are fair in their rule, their families and what they are responsible for.')
card('muslim:1829', 'Ibn Umar: every one of you is a shepherd and answerable for his flock: the ruler, the man for his family, the woman for her husband\'s home, and the servant for his master\'s property.')
card('muslim:1907', 'Umar ibn al-Khattab: actions are judged by intentions, and each person gets what he intended; emigration for Allah and His Messenger is for them, and emigration for worldly gain or a woman is for that.')
card('muslim:2017', 'Hudhayfah: Satan makes lawful the food over which Allah\'s name has not been mentioned; the Prophet seized the hands of a girl and a bedouin who reached for the food before he began.')
card('muslim:2018', 'Jabir: when a man mentions Allah\'s name on entering his house and while eating, Satan says there is no lodging or supper here for you; if he does not, Satan finds both.')
card('muslim:2109', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: the people who will be most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the makers of pictures.')
card('muslim:2137', 'Samurah ibn Jundub: the dearest words to Allah are four, SubhanAllah, Alhamdulillah, La ilaha illa Allah and Allahu akbar; and do not name your servants Yasar, Rabah, Najih or Aflah.')
card('muslim:2174', 'Anas: when two men passed as the Prophet walked with his wife, he told them who she was and said Satan moves through a person like blood.')
card('muslim:2187', 'Abu Hurayrah: the influence of the evil eye is real.')
card('muslim:2188', 'Ibn Abbas: the evil eye is real; if anything could overtake destiny it would be the evil eye, and when you are asked to wash, wash.')
card('muslim:2189', 'Aisha: Labid ibn al-Asam, of Banu Zuraiq, cast a spell on the Prophet so that he imagined doing things he had not done; Allah showed him in a dream what had been done and he was healed.')
card('muslim:2202', 'Uthman ibn Abi al-As: he complained of a pain in his body; the Prophet told him to place his hand on the place, say "Bismillah" three times and seven times "I seek refuge in Allah and His power from the evil of what I find and fear".')
card('muslim:223', 'Abu Malik al-Ashari: cleanliness is half of faith, "Alhamdulillah" fills the scale, prayer is light, charity is proof, patience is illumination, and the Qur\'an is an argument for you or against you.')
card('muslim:224', 'Ibn Umar: the Prophet said no prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from stolen booty.')
card('muslim:2261', 'Abu Qatadah: a good dream is from Allah and a disliked dream from Satan; whoever sees one he dislikes should spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, and it will not harm him.')
card('muslim:245', 'Uthman ibn Affan: whoever performs wudu well, his sins come out of his body, even from under his fingernails.')
card('muslim:252', 'Abu Hurayrah: had it not been a hardship for the believers, the Prophet would have ordered them to use the toothstick at every prayer.')
card('muslim:2568', 'Thawban: whoever visits a sick person remains in the fruit-garden of Paradise until he returns.')
card('muslim:257', 'Abu Hurayrah: five things are of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails, plucking the underarm hair and trimming the moustache.')
card('muslim:2586', 'An-Numan ibn Bashir: believers in mutual love, mercy and compassion are like one body; when one limb aches the whole body responds with sleeplessness and fever.')
card('muslim:2588', 'Abu Hurayrah: charity does not decrease wealth; Allah increases in honour the one who forgives, and raises the one who is humble for His sake.')
card('muslim:2589', 'Abu Hurayrah: backbiting is mentioning your brother in a way he dislikes; if what you say is true it is backbiting, and if it is false it is slander.')
card('muslim:259', 'Ibn Umar: the Prophet said to trim the moustache closely and let the beard grow.')
card('muslim:2605', 'Umm Kulthum bint Uqba: the Prophet said the one who reconciles people by speaking good or conveying good is not a liar.')
card('muslim:2607', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: truthfulness leads to righteousness and righteousness to Paradise; lying leads to wickedness and wickedness to the Fire.')
card('muslim:2609', 'Abu Hurayrah: the strong man is not the one who wrestles well, but the one who controls himself when angry.')
card('muslim:2625', 'Ibn Umar: Jibril kept urging the Prophet to be kind to the neighbour until he thought he would make the neighbour an heir.')
card('muslim:2643', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: a person\'s constituents are gathered for forty days in the womb, then a clot for forty days, then a lump of flesh for forty days; then an angel is sent to write provision, lifespan, deeds and whether he will be wretched or happy.')
card('muslim:2664', 'Abu Hurayrah: a strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than a weak one, yet both have good; strive for what benefits you, seek Allah\'s help, and do not say "if only" when misfortune comes.')
card('muslim:2675', 'Abu Hurayrah, reporting Allah\'s words: "I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me"; whoever draws near by a hand-span, Allah draws near by an arm\'s length.')
card('muslim:2698', 'Mus\'ab ibn Sad: the Prophet asked whether any of you cannot earn a thousand good deeds a day; whoever says "SubhanAllah" a hundred times has a thousand good deeds recorded or a thousand sins wiped away.')
card('muslim:2710', 'Al-Bara ibn Azib: at bedtime make wudu as for prayer, lie on your right side and say the supplication "O Allah, I submit my face to You"; if you die that night you die upon the fitrah (Islam).')
card('muslim:2711', 'Al-Bara: at bedtime the Prophet said "In Your name, O Allah, I live and die", and on waking "Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection".')
card('muslim:2814', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: everyone has a companion from the jinn assigned to him; the Prophet said he too has one, but Allah helped him against it, so it only commands him to good.')
card('muslim:2824', 'Abu Hurayrah, reporting Allah\'s words: "I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard and no heart has imagined."')
card('muslim:2844', 'Abu Hurayrah: the Companions heard a great crash; the Prophet said it was a stone thrown into Hell seventy years ago which had just reached the bottom.')
card('muslim:2999', 'Suhayb: the believer\'s affair is all good: if good befalls him he is grateful and that is good for him, and if harm befalls him he is patient and that is good for him.')
card('muslim:362', 'Abu Hurayrah: if one of you feels something in his stomach and is unsure whether anything has come out, he should not leave the mosque unless he hears a sound or smells something.')
card('muslim:384', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: when you hear the muadhdhin, repeat what he says, then send blessings on me and ask Allah for the wasila (a rank in Paradise) for me; whoever asks it for me, my intercession is guaranteed for him.')
card('muslim:408', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever sends blessings on me once, Allah sends blessings on him ten times.')
card('muslim:442', 'Ibn Umar: when your women ask permission to go to the mosque, do not prevent them.')
card('muslim:47', 'Abu Hurayrah: whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or keep silent, be kind to his neighbour and honour his guest.')
card('muslim:54', 'Abu Hurayrah: you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another; the Prophet recommended spreading the greeting of peace to foster that love.')
card('muslim:572', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: the Prophet prayed and was told something in the prayer was different; he turned to the qibla, made two prostrations and ended with the salam, saying he was a human who forgets.')
card('muslim:588', 'Abu Hurayrah: after the final tashahhud seek refuge in Allah from four things: the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of life and death, and the trial of the Antichrist (Dajjal).')
card('muslim:59', 'Abu Hurayrah: the signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is trusted he betrays.')
card('muslim:650', 'Ibn Umar: prayer in congregation is twenty-seven degrees more excellent than prayer said alone.')
card('muslim:656', 'Uthman ibn Affan: whoever prays Isha in congregation is as if he prayed half the night, and whoever prays Fajr in congregation is as if he prayed the whole night.')
card('muslim:713', 'Abu Usayd: on entering the mosque say "O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy", and on leaving say "O Allah, I ask You for Your bounty".')
card('muslim:761', 'Aisha: the Prophet prayed in the mosque at night and people joined him on successive nights; he stayed away on the third or fourth night, fearing the prayer would become obligatory for them.')
card('muslim:798', 'Aisha: the one who recites the Qur\'an skilfully is with the noble, obedient angels, and the one who falters and finds it hard has a double reward.')
card('muslim:804', 'Abu Umamah: recite the Qur\'an, for on the Day of Resurrection it will come as an intercessor for its reciters; recite al-Baqarah and Al Imran, which will come like clouds or flocks of birds pleading for their reciters.')
card('muslim:808', 'Abu Masud: whoever recites the last two verses of Surat al-Baqarah at night, they will be enough for him.')
card('muslim:867', 'Jabir: the Prophet\'s Friday sermon, in which he said the best speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, and the worst of matters are those newly invented.')
card('muslim:87', 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah: the Prophet named the gravest sins as associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and false testimony or false speech.')
card('muslim:892', 'Aisha: on Eid two girls sang songs of Buath at her house; Abu Bakr objected but the Prophet said every people has a festival and this is ours.')
card('muslim:899', 'Aisha: when a wind or dark cloud came the Prophet was uneasy, fearing it might be punishment for his people, and he was relieved when it rained.')
card('muslim:918', 'Umm Salamah: whoever is struck by a calamity and says "We belong to Allah and to Him we return; O Allah, reward me in my affliction and give me something better", Allah gives him something better.')
card('muslim:926', 'Anas: patience is at the first blow; the Prophet told a woman weeping for her child to fear Allah and be patient.')
card('muslim:944', 'Abu Hurayrah: make haste with the funeral; if the dead person was righteous you are sending him to good, and if not you are putting an evil from your necks.')
card('muslim:977', 'Buraydah: the Prophet said he had forbidden visiting graves but now allowed it, and lifted earlier restrictions on keeping sacrificial meat and on certain drinking vessels, while intoxicants stay forbidden.')

card('tirmidhi:1085', 'Abu Hatim al-Muzani: when someone whose religion and character you are pleased with proposes, marry him (your daughter or ward) to him, otherwise there will be turmoil and corruption in the land.')
card('tirmidhi:1862', 'Abdullah ibn Umar: whoever drinks intoxicants, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he repents Allah accepts his repentance.')
card('tirmidhi:1924', 'Abdullah ibn Amr: the merciful are shown mercy by Ar-Rahman; be merciful to those on earth and the One above the heavens will be merciful to you; whoever keeps the ties of kinship, Allah keeps ties with him.')
card('tirmidhi:1956', 'Abu Dharr: smiling in your brother\'s face is charity, enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity, guiding a lost man, removing a stone or thorn from the road, and pouring from your bucket into your brother\'s bucket are charity.')
card('tirmidhi:2307', 'Abu Hurayrah: remember often the destroyer of pleasures, meaning death.')
card('tirmidhi:2344', 'Umar ibn al-Khattab: if you relied on Allah as He should be relied on, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds, which go out hungry in the morning and return full.')
card('tirmidhi:2875', 'Abu Hurayrah: the Prophet told Ubayy ibn Kab that nothing like Surat al-Fatihah has been revealed in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms or the Qur\'an.')
card('tirmidhi:2887', 'Anas: everything has a heart and the heart of the Qur\'an is Ya Sin; whoever recites it, Allah writes for him the reward of reciting the Qur\'an ten times. (Graded weak.)')
card('tirmidhi:2890', 'Ibn Abbas: a Companion heard someone reciting Surat al-Mulk from a grave; the Prophet said it is the defender and the deliverer from the punishment of the grave. (Graded weak.)')
card('tirmidhi:2891', 'Abu Hurayrah: there is a surah of thirty verses that intercedes for its reciter until he is forgiven, Tabarak, Surat al-Mulk.')
card('tirmidhi:2910', 'Abdullah ibn Masud: whoever recites a letter from Allah\'s Book gets a good deed, and each good deed is multiplied by ten; Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter and Mim is a letter.')
card('tirmidhi:3372', 'An-Numan ibn Bashir: the Prophet said supplication (dua) is worship, and recited "Call upon Me, I will respond to you" (Qur\'an 40:60).')
card('tirmidhi:3388', 'Uthman ibn Affan: whoever says three times morning and evening "In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can harm, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing", nothing will harm him.')
card('tirmidhi:3431', 'Umar: whoever sees a person afflicted and says "Praise be to Allah who saved me from what He tested you with and favoured me over many of His creation", will be spared that affliction. (Graded weak.)')
card('tirmidhi:3451', 'Talhah ibn Ubaydullah: on seeing the new moon the Prophet said "O Allah, bring it over us with blessing and faith, with safety and Islam; my Lord and your Lord is Allah". (Graded weak.)')
card('tirmidhi:3458', 'Muadh ibn Anas: whoever eats food and says "Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided it without any might or power from me", his past sins are forgiven.')
card('tirmidhi:3524', 'Anas: when something distressed him the Prophet would say "O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining, in Your mercy I seek relief".')
card('tirmidhi:745', 'Aisha: the Prophet used to take care to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.')
card('tirmidhi:747', 'Abu Hurayrah: deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday, and the Prophet loved that his deeds be presented while he was fasting.')
card('tirmidhi:807', 'Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani: whoever provides a fasting person with food to break his fast gets the same reward as the fasting person, without reducing his reward.')
card('tirmidhi:85', 'Qays ibn Talq, from his father: asked about touching one\'s private part, the Prophet said it is only a piece of one\'s flesh.')
card('tirmidhi:92', 'Kabshah bint Kab: Abu Qatadah let a cat drink from the water she poured for his wudu, and said the Prophet said cats are not impure, they are among those who go about among you.')
